From fc758f03707d1b4a939b5835150d59b36850c1bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: oddlyspaced <oddlyspaced1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:32:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: allow the stock HAL to replace this one

metroid ships Nothing's stock thermal HAL as a prebuilt because it carries
their shell_max mapping and thresholds. It installs under the same stem, so
both would generate the same install rule and ninja fails with dupbuild=err.

Guard this module behind soong_config metroid.stock_thermal, mirroring what
vendor/qcom/opensource/vibrator already does for the QTI vibrator service.
Filtering PRODUCT_PACKAGES does not work -- the module is pulled in
independently of that list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I63ed94713c97f307bf2d7db37f0eaa1162659c24
---
 Android.bp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 8746923..a397370 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -3,6 +3,15 @@ soong_namespace {
 
 cc_binary {
 	name: "android.hardware.thermal-service.qti",
+	// metroid ships the stock Nothing thermal HAL as a prebuilt
+	// (android.hardware.thermal-service.qti.stock) because it carries Nothing's
+	// shell_max mapping and thresholds. It installs under the same stem, so both
+	// would generate the same install rule and ninja fails with dupbuild=err.
+	// Mirrors the soong_config guard already used for the QTI vibrator service.
+	enabled: select(soong_config_variable("metroid", "stock_thermal"), {
+		true: false,
+		default: true,
+	}),
 	relative_install_path: "hw",
 	init_rc: ["android.hardware.thermal-service.qti.rc"],
 	vintf_fragments: ["android.hardware.thermal-service.qti.xml"],
-- 
